    "body_tail": "ove the utils.legacy import and the shout() call; add 'from utils.text import slugify' (matching the existing import style) and apply slugify where shout was used so greet() still returns the greeting string.\n- Delete src/utils/legacy.py entirely.\n- Grep the repo (especially src/) for any remaining references to 'legacy' or 'shout' to confirm none are left.\n- Leave all changes uncommitted in the working tree.\n\n**Risks:**\n- Import style in src/app.py may be relative ('from .utils.text import slugify') or absolute; match existing conventions to avoid ImportError.\n- Unicode vs ASCII alphanumerics: decide based on expected tests; the examples only cover ASCII, so [^a-z0-9] after lowercasing is the safe interpretation.\n- Deleting legacy.py could break other modules if hidden references exist; verify with a repo-wide search before finishing.\n- greet() must still return a greeting string; ensure slugify is applied to the same value shout was used on, not to the whole greeting in a way that changes expected output.\n\n**Files (hints):** `src/utils/text.py`, `src/app.py`, `src/utils/legacy.py`\n## Implementation\n- Harness: **claude-sdk-lane** \u00b7 model glm-5.3-flash\n- Fallbacks: claude-code\n- Budget class: standard\n- Commit cycles: 3\n- Selection reason: default\n\n---\n\n**Plan digest:** `ec554615d6391e117d248a9f61e6fbace74ad51f19e0eb296ab932f6d940000b`\n\nApprove this exact plan by commenting `@forge /go 04bca389d69e4d4c9ef0ee223a0ed65e`.\n\nApprovers: @forcewake.\n\n*This is an automated message.*",
